cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "A Variational Control Framework for Optimal Portfolio Rebalancing Under Transaction Costs"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible discrete-time dynamic-programming study of portfolio
  rebalancing under proportional transaction costs. Exploiting CRRA
  homogeneity the value function reduces to one dimension; backward induction
  recovers the classical no-trade region and its comparative statics. A small
  neural network trained to imitate the optimal policy attains low
  action-space error yet is the worst performer economically, because a smooth
  regressor cannot represent the no-trade region and therefore over-trades.
